{
  "requirement": "`AgentSettings<D>` identifies the configurations a domain can use in its cache.\nTBV implements this sealed trait for `AgentConfig` and `AgentWithTools<D>`.\n\n```rust,ignore\npub trait AgentSettings<D: Domain>: Settings<D> { }\n```",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The tests adequately cover the three obligations in `requirements.sdk.graph.agent-harness.AgentSettings`.\n\n**Obligations derived from the text**\n1. `AgentSettings<D>` is a sealed trait, so third parties cannot implement it.\n2. `AgentConfig` implements it.\n3. `AgentWithTools<D>` implements it.\n4. Types implementing it are the configurations a domain can use in its cache. This is the `ValidationCache::with_agent(impl AgentSettings<D>)` entry point.\n\n**Test mapping**\n- **Sealing:** the `compile_fail` doctest on `crates/trust-but-verify/src/agent/config.rs#trait[AgentSettings]` is marked `{test}`. It tries `impl<D: Domain> AgentSettings<D> for ThirdPartyConfig {}` from outside the crate, through the public `trust_but_verify::agent` path.\n  - The supertrait `sealed::Settings` lives in `pub(crate) mod sealed` in `domain_tools.rs`. A foreign type therefore cannot satisfy it, and the doctest fails to compile for that reason.\n  - A `compile_fail` doctest accepts any compile error. That is a minor weakness. The imports are public and the snippet is otherwise well-formed, so the sealing is the only plausible failure.\n- **`AgentConfig` accepted:** `crates/trust-but-verify/src/agent/configured.rs#mod[tests]/fn[bedrock_configuration_attaches_to_a_cache_without_being_persisted]` passes an `AgentConfig::Bedrock(..)` to `ValidationCache::with_agent`.\n  - It asserts the cache's `agent.backend` equals the config.\n  - It asserts the agent is shared across clones.\n  - It runs a validation through the cache.\n  - It checks the config is not persisted.\n- **`AgentWithTools<D>` accepted:** `crates/trust-but-verify/src/agent/configured.rs#mod[tests]/fn[registered_tools_use_the_current_context_and_ordinary_node_ids]` passes `backend.with_tool(..).with_tool(..)` to `with_agent`. That value is an `AgentWithTools<D>`.\n  - It then asks a question through the cache.\n  - It asserts the registered tools reach the backend request in order, and that a different tool set gives a different tool list.\n  - Both the config and the tools therefore flow into the cache's agent.\n\nEvery obligation has a marked test with outcome assertions. I found no unacknowledged gap.",
  "references": "cec8dc27c3b2606c94129fd6e5a30835b88f6c749b7486e187768c03410c8bbd",
